# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which keeps .git -- 57 MB of
# the repo's 65 MB. Excluding it and the non-runtime directories takes the upload
# to roughly 2 MB, which is the difference between a build that starts immediately
# and one that spends a minute on transfer.
#
# Anything the running app reads must NOT be listed here: app.py, sage/, static/,
# profiles/, web/ and docs_snapshot.json all ship.

.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.devcontainer/

# Development-only trees. None of these are imported at runtime.
tests/
tools/
evals/
report/

# `docs/` is NOT a development tree -- it is the primary corpus. `profiles/rcc.toml`
# indexes it at weight 1.15, ABOVE the scraped `web/` pages, so an image built without
# it answers every User Guide question from marketing copy or not at all. What is
# excluded is only the 42 MB of screenshots the markdown links to: the reader follows
# a citation to docs.rcc.uchicago.edu and sees the picture there, and the source is
# declared `extensions = [".md"]`, so nothing in the image ever opens them.
# 72 .md files, 767 KB, ship; 141 images stay behind.
docs/**/*.png
docs/**/*.jpg
docs/**/*.jpeg
docs/**/*.pptx

# Local artifacts
.doc-backups/
.user-guide/
refresh-docs.log
*.jsonl
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/

# Never build a key into an image.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
